    <briefdescription>
<para>A suitably aligned and sized character array member which can hold elements of any type. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This template is equivalent to std::aligned_union_t&lt;1, ...&gt;, but we cannot use it due to a bug in the MSVC x86 compiler: <ulink url="https://github.com/microsoft/STL/issues/1533">https://github.com/microsoft/STL/issues/1533</ulink> Using <computeroutput>alignas</computeroutput> here works around the bug. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
